    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Lawrence Butler** (72.82) and **Jonathan Aranda** (70.47) emerge as our definitive anchors. **Lawrence Butler** benefits from an ideal confluence of a favorable matchup against Rocker and a significant park boost, while **Jonathan Aranda** exploits a strong 4.91 xERA from Bassitt combined with a high-leverage #2 spot in the order. Both players are well-positioned to drive our counting stats in 5x5 categories, benefiting from optimized platoon alignments that elevate their ceilings well above their base ATC projections. While **Gleyber Torres** (59.94) and **Zack Gelof** (57.85) provide solid secondary support, we are counting on the primary duo to provide the bulk of our offensive production against these vulnerable arms.\n\nThe decision to bench **Braden Montgomery** (39.41) was the most difficult call of the morning. While he carries significant intrigue, the unfavorable SP skill profile of Jobe (3.28 xERA) combined with the rigidity of our 40-point \"Zebras Floor\" mandate kept him off the active roster; he remains a high-variance asset we\u2019ll monitor closely for future starts. Conversely, **Jung Hoo Lee** (45.16) and **JJ Bleday** (48.36) are starting despite lower scores because they cleared our marginal threshold and retain potential for contribution in SB or R, respectively. We continue to monitor the status of **Will Smith**, who remains sidelined on the IL, while the inactivity of **Justin Crawford** today is mitigated by our current positional depth. \n\nWe must remain vigilant regarding the volatile matchups for **Cal Raleigh** and **Brendan Donovan** against Lambert; while their scores are respectable, they are facing an SP with enough variance to potentially deflate their production if the early innings go south. Additionally, while we are confident in **Daulton Varsho** (56.67) and **Masyn Winn** (51.35), we are keeping a close eye on the wind and park factors impacting the latter, as his reliance on speed makes him a top-tier priority in our stolen base hunt. If any late-breaking lineup changes force a pivot, we have sufficient depth on the bench to ensure no empty slots remain, maximizing our efficiency per game cap as we push through the mid-August stretch.",
